  "worked_solution": "Since our cubic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=3,$ ${x}_{2}=3,$ and ${x}_{3}=-2,$ and the coefficient of the cubic term is $a=5,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3}) & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x-(-2)) \\\\  & =5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5(x-3)(x-3)(x+2) & =5({x}^{2}-6x+9)(x+2) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}-12x+9x+18) \\\\  & =5({x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-3x+18) \\\\  & =5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=5{x}^{3}-20{x}^{2}-15x+90.$",
